Translation patch: keystore2::legacy_blob::LegacyBlobLoader::{extract_legacy_alias, remove_user_dir_if_empty, remove_super_key}

Change: keystore2/src/legacy_blob.rs: five calls to `Result::ok` are written without it, each on its own line. `x.ok();` used as a statement becomes `let _ = x;`, `r.ok().unwrap_or(false)` becomes `matches!(r, Ok(true))`, and `r.ok()` as a value becomes `match r { Ok(alias) => Some(alias), Err(_) => None }`.
Why: Aeneas translates `Result::ok` to an axiom named `core.result.Result.ok`. Inside the namespace `core.result.Result`, that name captures the `ok` of the Aeneas monad, so the translation of `Result::or_else` no longer builds in Lean (Aeneas issue #1554, open at the pinned release). These three functions are the only ones in the translated part of the crate that call `Result::ok`.
Behaviour: unchanged. Each rewritten expression has the same value and the same effects, in the same order, as the original; no panic is added or removed.
Classification: B
Assumptions: none.
Obligations: fork === upstream: each rewritten function behaves as the original on every input.
Evidence: an independent equivalence review by three reviewers, accepted on 2 of 3; summarised in formal/EXTRACTION-ISSUES.md.
Independent: yes

